  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5502.04 Review of Registration Requirement",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5502.04 Review of Registration Requirement.\n\n(a) Any sexual offender or offender against children who is required to register pursuant to RSA 651-B:1, V(c) or RSA 651-B:1, VII(d), may request in writing that the division review his or her registration requirement when he or she has a good faith belief that he or she is no longer required to register pursuant to the law in the jurisdiction where the offense occurred.\n\n(b) Upon receipt of a request pursuant to (a) above, the division shall review the sexual offender or offender against children’s registration requirements in accordance with RSA 651-B and these rules.\n\nSource. #10121, eff 4-25-12; ss by #13504, eff 12-9-22",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5500.html"
